\"ul\",\"145f274061b4-parent\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"145f274061b4\",{\"children\":[\"OpenAI: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"d4cb78ed1e751\",{\"href\":\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-o3-and-o4-mini/\",\"children\":[\"o3 launch post\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"d4cb78ed1e753\",{\"href\":\"https://cdn.openai.com/pdf/2221c875-02dc-4789-800b-e7758f3722c1/o3-and-o4-mini-system-card.pdf\",\"children\":[\"o3 system card\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"769272cdfa84\",{\"children\":[\"Gemini: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"a00d571477611\",{\"href\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/model-cards/documents/gemini-2.5-pro.pdf\",\"children\":[\"2.5 Pro model card\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"748e1f39641d\",{\"children\":[\"Claude: \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"6a0f74ba11201\",{\"href\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-3-7-sonnet\",\"children\":[\"Sonnet 3.7 launch post\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"6a0f74ba11203\",{\"href\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-4\",\"children\":[\"Claude 4 launch post\"]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"8a97d98e47a7\",{\"children\":[\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"165cf514a70d\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"21cb703f6fb70\",{\"children\":[\"Benchmark reporting\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"6f62df0e44cd\",{\"children\":[\"Claude models are hybrid reasoning models. The benchmarks reported in this blog post show the highest scores achieved with or without extended thinking. We’ve noted below for each result whether extended thinking was used:\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"e5a2034c4d85-parent\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"e5a2034c4d85\",{\"children\":[\"No extended thinking: SWE-bench Verified, Terminal-Bench\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4333873ad04a\",{\"children\":[\"The following benchmarks were reported with extended thinking (up to 64K tokens): TAU-bench, GPQA Diamond, MMMLU, MMMU, AIME\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"aa11968476d8\",{\"children\":[\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"38139460d862\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"96c509573cb50\",{\"children\":[\"TAU-bench methodology\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"105bf0467b03\",{\"children\":[\"Scores were achieved with a prompt addendum to both the Airline and Retail Agent Policy instructing Claude to better leverage its reasoning abilities while using extended thinking with tool use. The model is encouraged to write down its thoughts as it solves the problem distinct from our usual thinking mode, during the multi-turn trajectories to best leverage its reasoning abilities. To accommodate the additional steps Claude incurs by utilizing more thinking, the maximum number of steps (counted by model completions) was increased from 30 to 100 (most trajectories completed under 30 steps with only one trajectory reaching above 50 steps).\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"79cbb401310f\",{\"children\":[\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"dfd5ffa24db3\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"f33ffeb5a5bc0\",{\"children\":[\"SWE-bench methodology\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"610be5331163\",{\"children\":[\"For the Claude 4 family of models, we continue to use the same simple scaffold that equips the model with solely the two tools described in our prior releases \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"72a072fb5a721\",{\"href\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/swe-bench-sonnet\",\"children\":[\"here\"]}],\"—a bash tool, and a file editing tool that operates via string replacements. We no longer include the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"72a072fb5a723\",{\"href\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/claude-think-tool\",\"children\":[\"third ‘planning tool’\"]}],\" used by Claude 3.7 Sonnet. On all Claude 4 models, we report scores out of the full 500 problems. Scores for OpenAI models are reported out of a \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"72a072fb5a725\",{\"href\":\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-4-1/\",\"children\":[\"477 problem subset\"]}],\".\"]}]]]}],\"$L22\"]}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"LandingPageSection-module-scss-module__ZSMdoa__root\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"data-theme\":\"ivory\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"page-wrapper\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"SectionIntro-module-scss-module__i9TRza__root LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__intro\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"headline-4 SectionIntro-module-scss-module__i9TRza__title\",\"children\":\"Related content\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__root\",\"children\":[false,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__items LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__threeItems\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__item\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"headline-6\",\"children\":\"2026 Usage Policy update\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"body-3 serif\",\"children\":\"We’re publishing a new version of our Usage Policy. In this post, we summarize the changes we’ve made.\"}],[\"$\",\"$L23\",null,{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__cta\",\"link\":{\"text\":\"Read more\",\"url\":\"/news/2026-usage-policy-update\"},\"ctaPosition\":\"linkGrid\",\"icon\":[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"fill\":\"currentColor\"}],\"iconPosition\":\"right\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__item\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"headline-6\",\"children\":\"Building on our commitment to American scientific discovery\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"body-3 serif\",\"children\":\"Anthropic is committing $150 million over three years to the Genesis Mission, a federal initiative to accelerate scientific and technological discovery through AI. \"}],[\"$\",\"$L23\",null,{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__cta\",\"link\":{\"text\":\"Read more\",\"url\":\"/news/genesis-mission-commitment\"},\"ctaPosition\":\"linkGrid\",\"icon\":[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"fill\":\"currentColor\"}],\"iconPosition\":\"right\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"LinkGrid-module-scss-module__wTN57W__i